# Phase 88 plan 88-13 (88-13-14-RESEARCH.md G4): Git for Windows checks out with
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites every tracked text file to CRLF.
# The canary and byte-lock tests compare a `git show <sha>` blob (always LF) against the
# working tree, and the agent/skill compilers split on '\n'. Pin the working tree to LF.
# NO `git add --renormalize` was run: every tracked blob is byte-identical to before.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never translated, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary

# Blobs git has already classified as binary or as CRLF-stored. Marking them keeps
# `* text=auto eol=lf` from changing their bytes on the next `git add`.
